GLM_KV_Q4_STAGE_B.patch - stage B of the GLM latent q4_0 work (all-or-nothing; cut against HEAD 56f1b72).

Generator rules for the next regen (the two things that bite):
- glm_fast.hpp: the glm_lat_types.hpp include is ALREADY at line 17 (the stage-A compile fix moved it out
  of the /// doc comment and out of namespace glmf; committed in 56f1b72).  This patch adds NO include in
  glm_fast.hpp and must NEVER re-emit one - a second copy at the old site is exactly the stage-A bug that
  left lat8_rec_bytes undefined.  The include hunk for glm_fast.hpp is DONE; do not regenerate it.
- LatType is written UNQUALIFIED in the glm_model.hpp / glm_model.cu hunks (LatType::q4_0 etc.).  That
  compiles only because glm_model.hpp carries
      using LatType = strata::kernels::glmf::LatType;
  at line 43 (the stage-A fix, also committed in 56f1b72).  Regenerating from a tree without that alias
  yields six compile errors - qualify the spellings or confirm the alias first.
- generate.cpp is untouched (the __DATE__ literal fix lives in HEAD; stage B has nothing there).

Cache-state note: this patch flips lat_records_ = lat_type_ (all-or-nothing).  STRATA_STATE_SIGNATURE is
content-derived and changes with it, so stage-A int8 slots refuse by identity+digest on the first boot and
are re-recorded.  q4_0 requires kv_lora == 512 exactly (loud refusal at load otherwise); on HIP builds
q4_0 loudly falls back to truthful INT8 records.
